  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "After Fang Yuan is pushed out of the light, Qi clan Gu Immortals take the result as hope: he stays outside the gatehouse, and they only need to deal with Bai Ning Bing. One of them calls her Bai Xiang killer move troublesome, and says their Qi Xiang true inheritance is not weak either.",
      "chapters": [
        1637
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "fac_qi_clan",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_bai_ning_bing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Qi Xiang was one of the Heaven Surveying Five Xiangs, and Qi clan cultivates qi path primarily because of him.",
      "chapters": [
        1035
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan names Qi Xiang, Bai Xiang, Xue Xiang, Ni Xiang, and Chi Xiang as those Five Xiangs, notes their gatehouse fused all five, and assigns Qi Xiang to qi path. Familiar face briefly steadies Bai Xiang’s blue light for him, but the other four Xiang lights still reject him and push him out. He judges blood path, earth path, and food path workable from his own foundation, and ice path already covered because Bai Ning Bing’s Bai Xiang true inheritance deceived the blue light, so his only remaining obstacle at that gatehouse is Qi Xiang’s power. Qi path attainment and qi path inheritances are his weak point there, and he plans to force a way through with the light of wisdom.",
      "chapters": [
        1637
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
